WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:01.980
Movies: they're everywhere.

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:06.790
With multiple new releases coming out every
single day, there's just no way anybody has

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:08.760
the time or money to see all of them.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:13.000
Which is too bad, because it means that a
lot of really good films go completely under

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:13.700
the radar.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.199
Heck, you may not have even heard of some
of the best films of the year!

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.100
Don't worry, though, because we've got your
back.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.440
Here's a look at some of the brilliant movies
of 2017 you totally missed.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:24.940
Prevenge

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.580
Ask anyone who's ever been pregnant, and they'll
tell you that the whole "creating another

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.980
human with your own body" thing isn't easy.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:37.019
Back pain, swollen feet, and a rollercoaster
of emotions are enough to make even the most

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.080
calm people go a little crazy.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:44.360
But in Prevenge, that pregnancy-induced madness
quickly turns... to murder.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:49.140
Writer/director Alice Lowe plays Ruth, a pregnant
woman grappling with the death of her partner.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:54.220
As her due date nears, Ruth begins listening
to the menacing supernatural thoughts of her

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.480
unborn child, and starts to believe the world
should be held accountable for ultimately

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.520
leaving her baby without a father.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:05.859
Cue a revenge-fueled killing spree that leads
Ruth to reevaluate each piece of her wildly

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:07.020
fragmented life.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:13.180
"Just so that you know you have absolutely
no control over your mind or your body anymore.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.540
This one does."

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:19.440
Oh, and that's no prosthetic belly there:
Lowe was actually in her third trimester when

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:20.620
she filmed Prevenge.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.000
Talk about Method acting!

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:23.460
Chuck

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.640
Once upon a time there was a regular guy named
Chuck Wepner who sold liquor and did some

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.679
prizefighting on the side for cash to support
his family.

00:01:31.679 --> 00:01:37.249
Then, one day in 1975, he was cherry-picked
from a sea of boxers to go glove-to-glove

00:01:37.249 --> 00:01:40.940
with one of the world's greatest athletes:
boxing legend Muhammad Ali.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:46.580
As most film fans know, Wepner's amazing story
famously inspired the classic film Rocky.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:47.940
'How can I help you Mr. Wepner?"

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:49.520
"You follow boxing?"

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:50.880
"Rocky?"

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.260
"Tell Sly, Rocky's here."

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.020
"I can handle this."

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.840
But unlike the fictionalized Rocky, Chuck
aims to tell the true tale of this unlikely

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:03.960
sports hero, with Liev Schreiber in the lead
and a great cast including Naomi Watts backing

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:04.460
him up.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.280
The Lost City of Z

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:12.099
Charlie Hunnam, Robert Pattinson, Sienna Miller,
and the new Spider-Man himself Tom Holland

00:02:12.099 --> 00:02:16.780
teamed up for The Lost City of Z, a thought
provoking adventure tale about a group of

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:20.480
explorers searching the Amazon for a legendary
lost civilization.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.000
"I call it Zed.

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:25.660
The ultimate piece of the human puzzle!"

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:30.731
Unfortunately, The Lost City of Z opened the
same weekend as The Fate of the Furious, so

00:02:30.731 --> 00:02:35.500
pretty much nobody had any idea it existed,
and it vanished from the box office almost

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.320
instantly.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.500
The good news?

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.340
That gives you the opportunity to unearth
a cinematic lost treasure of your own.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.080
The Transfiguration

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:46.960
This one is definitely not your average vampire
thriller.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:51.560
The Transfiguration shifts its focus away
from classic vampire tales to the story a

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:56.849
young teen named Milo who shields himself
from the unfriendly outside world with a deep-rooted

00:02:56.849 --> 00:02:58.540
fascination with the undead.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:02.780
But that interest turns lethally obsessive
when he becomes friends with the troubled

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:07.760
Sophie, leading to a chilling slice-of-afterlife
indie horror flick that will leave you completely

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:08.420
transfixed.

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:11.240
"And you change a lot, after the first person
you kill.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:16.460
You change a lot more after… after one after
another?"

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:18.080
The Devil's Candy

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:23.240
Ethan Embry stars in this sinfully delicious
horror film about a tortured artist who blacks

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:27.780
out and wakes to discover he has painted a
horrifying portrait of pure evil.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:31.230
Has he been touched by some kind of holy - or
unholy - force?

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:32.950
Or is he simply going mad?

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:35.880
The only way to find out is to watch The Devil's
Candy for yourself.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.459
If you dare!

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.620
T2 Trainspotting

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:45.880
To anyone who's said sequels rarely stack
up, we counter with T2 Trainspotting, the

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:48.790
21-years-later follow-up to Danny Boyle's
classic Trainspotting.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:54.519
Two decades on, T2 peeks in on the life of
the gang from the original, with Begbie, Renton,

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:59.900
Spud and Sick Boy each in an unexpected - or
all too expected - place in their lives.

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:01.440
Can people really change?

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:04.000
Or is that just an illusion we sell ourselves?

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:08.049
Boyle's inventive sequel asks the questions,
but you may not like the answers.

00:04:08.049 --> 00:04:09.670
"Where did it all go wrong?

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:11.660
Hahaha."

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:13.480
"Where did it all go wrong?"

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:14.300
"Where did it all go wrong?"

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.140
"Where did it all go wrong?"

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:18.520
I Don't Feel at Home in This World Anymore

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:24.560
This Netflix exclusive release stars Elijah
Wood and Melanie Lynskey as a pair of eccentric

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:28.980
neighbors who embark on a quest to track down
the thieves who burgled her home.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:32.840
Their mission quickly melts into chaos and
violence as they frantically try to outwit

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:35.600
the pack of corrupt criminals following their
every move.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:41.100
I Don't Feel at Home in This World Anymore
bursts forward with an inventive, subversive,

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:46.060
slyly smart, and downright fun feel that'll
have you hollering in one scene and pondering

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.800
society's structure in the next.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.300
"All right tough guy, you had your chance."

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.460
"Ow ow."

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:57.100
"Oh God… are you OK?"

00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:58.800
Dig Two Graves

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:03.760
The brainchild of screenwriters Hunter Adams
and Jeremy Phillips, the indie horror outing

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:08.670
Dig Two Graves centers around 14-year-old
Jacqueline Mather, referred to by her more

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:10.300
masculine nickname "Jake."

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:15.220
Grieving for her recently deceased brother,
Jake is thrown for a loop when she's visited

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:18.820
by three strange men who say they can bring
him back to life.

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:21.300
"I'm not supposed to talk to strangers, so..

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:23.740
I'm Wyeth.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:28.320
Now that we know each other we're no longer
strangers."

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:29.480
Are they telling the truth?

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:32.260
What lengths will Jake have to go to see her
brother again?

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:36.130
And what does her grandfather, Sheriff Waterhouse,
have to do with it?

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:40.810
As Jake begins to contemplate an unthinkable
trade-off, dark secrets of her family's once-hidden

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:43.490
history rises to the surface.

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:48.530
Inspired by gothic motifs of grief and revenge,
and soaked with the uncertainty of an ambiguous

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:52.260
timeline, Dig Two Graves should captivate
discerning genre enthusiasts.

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:57.040
And though it didn't make any big waves at
the box office, given its tiny release, Dig

00:05:57.050 --> 00:06:01.880
Two Graves has been showered with acclaim
from critics, with RogerEbert.com calling

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:06.800
it an "uncommonly smart, well-made, and ultimately
touching meditation on grief."

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:08.600
Colossal

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:13.590
You'd expect a film with a title like Colossal
to be an overhyped summer tentpole, but this

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:18.230
pitch black sci-fi indie comedy came and went
without getting the media attention it deserved.

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:22.670
Colossal stars Oscar-winning actress Anne
Hathaway as Gloria, a woman in the throes

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:27.020
of a post-breakup existential limbo who's
shocked to realize she actually has bigger

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:30.690
problems than just curbing her drinking and
getting back on the dating scene.

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:35.840
Like, giant reptilian kaiju-sized problems
in the form of an enormous monster terrorizing

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:36.660
South Korea.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:40.940
These two things don't sound like they could
possibly be part of the same movie, but the

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:43.760
way Colossal connects them is just part of
the film's genius.

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:47.860
"I just feel like dancing so ah… so guess
which film this from huh?

00:06:47.980 --> 00:06:49.160
"F--- is going on?"

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:51.220
"Do you want to make any requests?

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:53.940
This does not last that long."

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:58.660
A distinctly unique take on the monster movie
genre boasting ultra fresh performances from

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:03.850
Hathaway and Jason Sudeikis, Colossal is decidedly
strange in the very best way.

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:08.340
From the Seoul street fights reminiscent of
Rock 'em Sock 'em Robots to the ultimate narrative

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:12.960
twist, here's a film weird and wild enough
to stretch your definition of what a creature

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:14.220
feature should be.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:15.600
Raw

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:20.460
This foreign horror flick is just as formidable
in English as it is in French.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:25.550
Raw, which was called Grave in its original
European release, starts off so simply it

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:27.300
may even elicit laughter.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:32.450
A movie all about a vegetarian adjusting to
college life amongst meat-eating peers?

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:33.800
Not exactly captivating.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:39.700
But writer-director Julia Ducournau practically
slaps you across the face with a rack of raw

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:41.380
ribs in the moments that follow.

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:46.510
Happy-go-lucky freshman and lifelong plant-eater
Justine has high hopes for veterinary school

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:49.210
and intends to be laser-focused on her studies.

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:54.690
However, her mind soon shifts to a different,
unexpected target: human flesh, the taste

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:58.730
she acquires after she's forced to eat raw
meat during a hazing ritual.

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:03.860
As Justine tries to make sense of her newfound
cannibalistic desires, Raw swerves down the

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:08.730
winding road of navigating college parties,
uppity professors, and the complexities of

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:09.860
sexual identity.

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:15.240
We won't spoil the ending, but we have a feeling
that Raw's third act is what catapulted it

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:19.920
into the laps of many adoring critics—and
made a few viewers fall out of their seats.

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:24.900
Bloody and brutal but oh-so bright, Raw is
a film you can really sink your teeth into.

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:25.900
Literally.

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:27.580
Land of Mine

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:34.400
After making big waves at the Toronto International
Film Festival and in Danish theaters in 2015,

00:08:34.409 --> 00:08:39.399
Land of Mine finally hit theaters in America
at the beginning of 2017, not that anyone

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:40.400
seemed to notice.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:43.480
That's a shame considering how gripping Land
of Mine is.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:48.060
Based on a true story, the film is set in
Denmark at the end of 1945.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:52.550
Freed from German occupation, the country
was still filled with thousands of hidden

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:53.240
land mines.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:54.540
Sgt.

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:58.660
Carl Rasmussen and his band of German prisoners
of war are tasked with clearing the explosives,

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:03.860
a job that brings into question justice, morality,
and vengeance in a single breath.

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:06.280
"(speaking Dutch)"

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:17.100
This historical drama earned itself a 2017
Oscar nomination for Best Foreign Language

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:22.610
Film, a standing ovation at TIFF, and the
title of best Danish film of 2015.

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:27.820
If Land of Mine is missing from your watchlist,
change that immediately—if not sooner.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:29.400
The Salesman

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:34.380
A twisty and intriguing drama from Iran, The
Salesman tells the story of Emad and Rana,

00:09:34.389 --> 00:09:39.560
a theater loving couple who set out to stage
a production of Arthur Miller's classic play

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:40.800
Death of a Salesman.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:45.460
After Rana is attacked, however, their lives
are upended as the need for revenge begins

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:47.380
to take center stage in their lives.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:48.400
"(Speaking Farsi)"

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:04.520
Lauded as an "ingenious cinematic use" of
the American stage, The Salesman's story-within-a-story

00:10:04.529 --> 00:10:09.120
brings to light questions about violence against
women, marriage, post-traumatic stress, death,

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:14.310
and the class system, and asks the audience
to work through them as the film runs on.

00:10:14.310 --> 00:10:18.730
Though The Salesman might've slipped past
you, it certainly wasn't lost with critics,

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:22.899
landing itself the Oscar for Best Foreign
Language Film at the 89th Academy Awards.

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:24.120
Thanks for watching!

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:27.120
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:29.459
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

